   \]

2. **Northward Flight (Next 2 hours at 18 mph):**
   \[
   \text{Distance} = 18 \, \text{mph} \times 2 \, \text{hours} = 36 \, \text{miles north}
   \]

3. **Final Southward Flight (Last 5 hours at 22 mph):**
   \[
   \text{Distance} = 22 \, \text{mph} \times 5 \, \text{hours} = 110 \, \text{miles south}
   \]

**Total Distance Traveled:**
\[
300 \, \text{miles south} + 36 \, \text{miles north} + 110 \, \text{miles south} = 446 \, \text{miles}
\]

Since the bird ends up at her southern home, the net displacement from the northern home is the sum of the southward and northward distances:
\[
300 \, \text{miles south} + 110 \, \text{miles south} - 36 \, \text{miles north} = 374 \, \text{miles south}
\]

#### Final Answer:
\[
\boxed{374}
\]
